[[0,1792110,0,2,0,2,"2017-04-14T01:30:00","skidmark-steve","",[],"","Microsoft raises pistol, pulls the trigger on Windows 7, 8 updates for new Intel, AMD chips. Some older chips get caught in the cross-fire too!","https://www.theregister.co.uk/2017/04/13/microsoft_kills_support_old_windows_on_new_chips/","technology"],[1,8774343,0,0,0,0,"2017-04-14T01:30:43","derram","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://archive.is/hiGTU\">https://archive.is/hiGTU</a> | <a href=\"https://vgy.me/0szIU2.png\">https://vgy.me/0szIU2.png</a> : \n</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Microsoft raises pistol, pulls the trigger on Windows 7, 8 updates for new Intel, AMD chips • The Register </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>&quot;Microsoft has cut software updates and tweaks for computers powered by Intel and AMD's latest-generation processors and running old versions of Windows.&quot;, &quot;The Redmond giant is no longer serving software fixes to PCs and other systems that run Windows 7 or Windows 8.1 on Intel's fresh new Kaby Lake or AMD's hot-off-the-fab Ryzen chips.&quot;, &quot;Microsoft argues this is all because it can't be bothered supporting the latest silicon, such as Intel's 7th-gen Core series, on anything other than Windows 10.&quot; </p>\n<p>'&quot;As new silicon generations are introduced, they will require the latest Windows platform at that time for support,&quot; Microsoft says on an FAQ page for its support lifecycle. ' </p>\n<p>'The ruling will no doubt irk some users – such as PC gamers – who have until now opted to run Windows 7 on their new machines and prefer the interface of the older OS over that of Windows 10. ' </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://vgy.me/AeTBAc.jpg\">This has been an automated message.</a></p>"],[1,8774344,0,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T01:31:00","skidmark-steve","",[],"<p>As well as being hilarious, this is a perfect example of why I will no longer waste my time fixing Microsoft's broken-by-design products for other computer users.</p>"],[2,8774465,8774344,2,0,2,"2017-04-14T01:44:00","Solstiare","",[],"<p>As Vulcan fleshes out, winhoze is going to have its gamer market share evaporate. I am planing on moving my environment to Mint/Ubuntu when the next round of upgrades hits. Microsoft's CEO can suck it.</p>"],[3,8774968,8774465,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T02:46:36","Bobo_Palermo","",[],"<p>I hope this is true. I need a gaming alternative.</p>"],[1,8778645,0,0,0,0,"2017-04-14T14:02:01","Ghetto_Shitlord","",[],"<p>I love their middle school playground headlines.</p>"]]
