[[0,1792121,0,3,0,3,"2017-04-14T01:38:13","BestDuckEver","",[],"","Yogoats in Oregon","https://i.imgtc.com/RX0q7pq.png","Goats"],[1,8774503,0,2,0,2,"2017-04-14T01:49:26","CANCEL-CAT-FACTS","",[],"<p>I would rather pet a goat than do yoga.</p>"],[1,8774656,0,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T02:08:03","Likeitirish","",[],"<p>Okay goats are awesome but come on...farm animals smell like shit. Literally they are doing yoga in a barn that smells like shit. The fuck is wrong with our society. I feel bad for those goats. </p>"],[2,8774681,8774656,2,0,2,"2017-04-14T02:11:58","BestDuckEver","",[],"<p>I was just about to say something similar to <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/CANCEL-CAT-FACTS\">@CANCEL-CAT-FACTS</a>, not only the smell, but the sanitary levels are most definitely questionable. </p>"],[3,8774757,8774681,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T02:20:19","Likeitirish","",[],"<p>hahaha. Goats eat anything and everything. And they walk around shitting like we do breathing. </p>"],[4,8774819,8774757,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T02:28:03","BestDuckEver","",[],"<p>Right? Though the head butting and knocking over would be entertaining to watch. So a little silver lining, lol.</p>"],[1,8774873,0,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T02:34:06","Kcpedogate","",[],"<p>This seems like it could get a little weird... if it hasn't already</p>"]]
[[0,1792122,0,3,0,3,"2017-04-14T01:38:21","Norm85","",[],"","Get a VPN today (Electronic Frontiers Australia)","https://www.efa.org.au/2017/04/13/get-a-vpn-today/","Australia"],[1,8776475,0,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T06:30:49","blipblipbeep","[e]",[],"<p>Sorry if this plug sounds rehearsed, Its not, its just that its my first VPN so I did quite a bit of investigating to feel safe.</p>\n<p>Just got <a href=\"https://windscribe.com/\">Windscribe</a> with free subscription. </p>\n<p>No credit card needed unless you want to use one of their plans, you need to supply an email to use vouchers tho It can be a throwaway as long as its active for a one time confirmation link. Vouchers can be used on their free service as well.</p>\n<p>Seems legit, Canadian based VPN with 5 end point locations for the free service and 24 (I think) for the paid service, says they don't keep logs and also block ads and tracking data as a part of their service. </p>\n<p>Most Internet reviews said they are the best and a relatively new service looking to impress and also have a fast ticket help service, I can't see why most would need it tho as it was seamless to get it up and running, I did need to load a windows TAP driver (that was an auto service and seemed legit as well) to get it running. </p>\n<p>I speed tested it and I was getting between 800kb and 1mb dl speeds, ping was in the 300s tho. </p>\n<p>There is more useful info about their service at their website. </p>\n<p>I searched for a voucher and found 50GBFREE as a voucher keyword for 50GB per month free download otherwise its 10GB per month, not sure how many are left, the search results did indicate that its been a common offer they have provided lately tho. There are also other perks for scouting people from twitter and facebook, I don't use either of those services though.</p>\n<p>So far I'm impressed, so this is me giving them an unprompted an off the books plug. K, I gave them a free plug for their free service, my job is done here.</p>\n<p>Ultimately, don't take my word for it, please do your own research and please let us know here if you have reason to believe this or any other VPN services should be avoided.</p>\n<p>Good hunting,</p>\n<p>peace... </p>"],[2,8777059,8776475,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T09:04:11","Norm85","",[],"<p>Thanks for sharing your information and thoughts. Researching, selecting and setting up a VPN is my Easter project.</p>\n<p>I think out of the 5 eyes countries, Canada and NZ are the best choices, but my current thought is to avoid these countries completely. <a href=\"https://thatoneprivacysite.net/vpn-comparison-chart/\">This tool</a> (which includes a 14 eyes criteria) from the EFA article is what I am using to narrow the list.</p>"],[3,8785962,8777059,1,0,1,"2017-04-15T03:55:56","blipblipbeep","",[],"<p>Np Norm mate, we do what we can. Yeah, It was my first go at it so I wanted to try a free one first. So far I'm pretty happy with it, I get what you mean about the 5 eyes thing though. I really just wanted to get one to give the bird to the hole data retention thing as I don't really need it, all the same it seemed like the best free one I could find and was so easy to setup and use that I may as well just keep rolling with it atm.</p>\n<p>With that said. I Was wondering if you wouldn't mind posting or PMing me your chosen VPN and why you chose it when you get one mate, I Wouldn't mind knowing about some of the other options around.</p>\n<p>Thanks for your reply norm mate :) Hope you have a great Easter holiday.</p>\n<p>Catch'ya next time,</p>\n<p>peace... </p>"]]
[[0,1792123,0,1,0,1,"2017-04-14T01:38:34","Samsquamch","",[],"","Syrian chemical attack victim hits out at CNN host Brooke Baldwin for trying to make him criticize Trump","http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-4393938/Syrian-chemical-attack-victim-hits-CNN-journalist.html","CNNFakeNews"],[1,8774486,0,0,0,0,"2017-04-14T01:46:44","derram","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://archive.is/WIqhi\">https://archive.is/WIqhi</a> | <a href=\"https://vgy.me/E9ZdHO.png\">https://vgy.me/E9ZdHO.png</a> : \n</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Syrian chemical attack victim hits out CNN journalist | Daily Mail Online </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>&quot;With all due respect, this is hypocrisy, if you really care, help us stay in our country. 'We don't want to become refugees, help us establish safe zones.&quot;, &quot;A Syrian man lashed out after being asked by a CNN reporter to criticize Donald Trump's refugee ban.&quot; </p>\n<p>'Anchor Brooke Baldwin attempted to make a point about acceptance of refugees while talking to Kassam Eid, who survived a 2013 chemical attack on Syria. ', &quot;Eid praised the President's action in firing missiles at Bashar al-Assad in retaliation for chemical attacks against his citizens on Tuesday.&quot; </p>\n<p>'Eid then went on to fully thank President Donald Trump, and say that he supports the efforts that he is making in the Middle East. ' </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://vgy.me/5OhPUU.jpg\">This has been an automated message.</a></p>"]]
